  "summary_en": "The Giant Canyon, formed by the Víðidalsá River, features the Kolufossar waterfall series at its entrance, with the waterfall on one side and the canyon on the other. It is a rare Icelandic spot where a canyon and waterfall coexist, offering a compact yet beautiful view. Parking is available for free, though the lot is small, so arrive early. After parking, head to the viewpoint to enjoy the scenery. No restroom facilities are provided on site. Allow about 60 minutes for a visit.",
